                <p class="w-95">Intermediate Bulk Containers (IBCs) and Offshore Tankers are compact, versatile units designed for the safe storage and transport of chemicals, oils, and hazardous liquids in offshore and industrial environments. Typically constructed from stainless steel or high-density polyethylene (HDPE), these containers feature a reinforced frame, lifting lugs, and forklift pockets for easy handling and mobility.</p>
                <p class="w-95 mb-0">IBCs range in capacity from 500 to 1,500 liters and include top manlids, discharge valves, and pressure relief systems for secure filling and emptying. Offshore tanks comply with IMDG, DNV 2.7-1, and UN certifications, making them ideal for marine and offshore chemical logistics where space efficiency and safety are critical.</p>
